  "result": "Excellent! All tests pass. Here's a summary of the tier-based discount implementation:\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **TIER_DISCOUNTS in customers.js**: Exported centralized configuration mapping tiers to percentages:\n   - gold: 5%\n   - silver: 2.5%\n   - standard: 0%\n\n2. **createInvoice enhancement**:\n   - Extracts and stores customer object to access tier\n   - For each line: if `discountPercent !== undefined`, uses explicit value; otherwise applies customer's tier discount\n   - This means explicit 0% overrides tier discount (important distinction)\n\n3. **addLine enhancement**:\n   - Same tier discount logic as createInvoice\n   - Gets customer to determine tier for new lines\n\n4. **Test coverage (106 total, all passing)**:\n   - Added 8 new tier discount tests covering:\n     - Each tier level (gold 5%, silver 2.5%, standard 0%)\n     - Explicit discount overriding tier\n     - Explicit 0% overriding tier (in both createInvoice and addLine)\n     - Mixed discounts in invoice totals\n   - Updated existing tests to account for tier discounts being applied automatically\n\nThe implementation correctly handles the key requirement: explicit discounts always win, but when a line has no discount specified, it inherits the customer's tier discount.",
